  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "The first experiment (config_044: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) achieved ~52% accuracy, which is modest. The most immediate uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation is actually contributing positively or introducing overfitting/instability relative to a simpler pooling strategy. Config_004 is a clean single-variable ablation (transformer → avgpool) holding all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion). If avgpool matches or exceeds the transformer result, it signals that the added complexity of transformer aggregation is not warranted and frees capacity to focus on other dimensions (fusion strategy, encoder choice). If the transformer clearly wins, it confirms that learned cross-profile attention is important and justifies keeping it in subsequent experiments. With 8 experiments remaining, resolving this architectural question early prevents wasting budget on variants built on a suboptimal aggregation backbone."
}

